This honesty is the project's strength. 2. What the formal work proves (that the IPVV confirms) Three results of the formal work are confirmed by the IPVV: 2.1 The σ-flip (AM0)

12
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:16,710
AM0 formalizes recognition as the σ-flip: T_rec changes σ (Sv→¬Sv), not the tuple (e, p, h, b, o). The IPVV confirms this at three registers (V1E/V1D/V3P): content unchanged, positioning changed.

13
00:02:16,710 --> 00:02:29,625
The AM0 formalization is the IPVV's own claim, made precise. [T] confirmed. 2.2 The exclusion-individuation (MEPIT) MEPIT formalizes individuation as the exclusion Eᵢ: Ω → (Sᵢ, Wᵢ).

14
00:02:29,625 --> 00:02:43,100
The IPVV confirms this: the apohana (the third power, IPK 1.3.7) is the power by which subject and world are jointly carved; MEPIT's five exclusions are the five kañcukas. [T] confirmed.

15
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:56,155
2.3 The rejection of the filter-model The recognition-formulation and AM0 reject the filter-model (M∞→Lᵢ→Mᵢ); the IPVV confirms it: "the Lord manifests the whole world from within himself" (V2G); "the one light

16
00:02:56,155 --> 00:03:09,700
rises, born of means, object and knower" (V3C). [T] confirmed. 3. What the formal work cannot prove (that prooof/observer-proofo establish) prooof and observer-proofo establish the limit of formal logic:

17
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:18,065
"Distinctions occur within local structures of contrast. Observers arise as dynamically maintained patterns that register such structures.

18
00:03:18,065 --> 00:03:23,815
Recognition begins when the observer includes its own operation within the dependence it has discovered...

19
00:03:23,815 --> 00:03:35,965
Whether the manifestness of that process is merely functional, intrinsically phenomenal, or an expression of universal reflexive consciousness remains the final open question." (observer-proofo)

20
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:42,645
That is: logic proves distinctions occur in local structures; it does not prove a universal consciousness.

21
00:03:42,645 --> 00:03:51,305
The step from "observers are relationally constituted patterns" to "one universal reflexive consciousness" requires premises beyond logic.

22
00:03:51,305 --> 00:03:58,745
The formal work is right about this. The IPVV does not claim otherwise — it does not offer a formal proof of the universal Lord.

23
00:03:58,745 --> 00:04:09,260
What it offers is a transcendental-causal argument (see the ultimate-proof and felt-to-ground essays), which the formal work does not address. 4. What the IPVV adds that the formal work cannot

24
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:21,440
The IPVV supplies what the formal work cannot: 1. The transcendental argument for the order-less support (V2O). The IPVV derives the need for an order-less, self-conscious support from the structure of ordered

25
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:29,145
experience. This is not a formal deduction (which cannot exist, per prooof), but it is an argument — a transcendental-causal one.

26
00:04:29,145 --> 00:04:39,510
The formal work shows logic cannot reach the universal; the IPVV shows experience (ordered, memory-bearing experience) requires an order-less support. 2.

27
00:04:39,510 --> 00:04:49,776
The non-constructed "I" (V2L). The IPVV argues the "I"-grasp is not a construction — the self-presence that every construction (including every self-model) presupposes.

28
00:04:49,776 --> 00:04:57,981
This is an argument the formal work does not provide: it grounds the possibility of recognition in a non-constructed self-grasp. 3.

29
00:04:57,981 --> 00:05:10,411
The felt register (the σ-flip as camatkāra). The IPVV ties the σ-flip to the felt — recognition is experienced as the joy of union (V3P). The formal work formalizes the σ-flip; the IPVV gives its felt face.

30
00:05:10,411 --> 00:05:18,471
The division of labor. The formal work establishes the structure (the σ-flip, the exclusion) and the limit (logic cannot prove the universal).

31
00:05:18,471 --> 00:05:26,686
The IPVV supplies the argument (the transcendental-causal chain) and the ground (the non-constructed "I", the order-less support).

32
00:05:26,686 --> 00:05:38,021
The two are complementary: the formal work sharpens the IPVV's claims; the IPVV supplies what the formal work cannot. 5. The ultimate formal proof of recognition: what it would require

33
00:05:38,021 --> 00:05:49,606
Can there be a formal proof of recognition? The honest answer, from the formal work and the IPVV together: - A formal proof of the σ-flip exists (AM0): recognition changes σ, not content.

34
00:05:49,606 --> 00:05:58,591
This is formal and confirmed by the IPVV. - A formal proof of the exclusion-individuation exists (MEPIT): subject and world are jointly carved by Eᵢ.

35
00:05:58,591 --> 00:06:07,611
This is formal and confirmed by the IPVV. - A formal proof of the universal Lord does NOT exist (prooof, observer-proofo): logic cannot force the one.

36
00:06:07,611 --> 00:06:13,056
The IPVV agrees — it offers a transcendental-causal argument, not a formal deduction.

37
00:06:13,056 --> 00:06:26,056
So the "ultimate formal proof of recognition" is: the σ-flip and the exclusion are formally provable; the universalization is not formally provable but is argued by the IPVV's transcendental-causal chain. The formal

38
00:06:26,056 --> 00:06:36,536
proof of recognition is complete up to the universalization; the universalization is the commitment that neither logic nor the IPVV can force. 6. The reconciliation

